{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeWedderburnGeneral","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeWedderburnGeneral","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeProductSurjective","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeCoset","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SchenstedRSKBurnside"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.heckeWedderburn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.heckeWedderburn","kind":"def","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeWedderburnGeneral.lean#L111-L116","doc":"The isomorphism itself. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.heckeProduct_bijective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.heckeProduct_bijective","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeWedderburnGeneral.lean#L95-L109","doc":"**The Wedderburn split of `H_{n+1}(q)`, for every `n`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.finrank_hecke_eq_factorial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.finrank_hecke_eq_factorial","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeWedderburnGeneral.lean#L72-L93","doc":"**`dim H_{n+1}(q) = (n+1)!`** — the Iwahori–Hecke basis theorem, both bounds.\n\nThe upper bound is `HeckeCoset.finrank_le_factorial`.  The lower bound is *not* proved by hand here:\nit is forced by the surjection onto a space of dimension `(n+1)!`.  So the Gröbner–Shirshov route\n(`qou-auq3`) is not on the critical path for this statement. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.finrank_blocks_eq_factorial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.finrank_blocks_eq_factorial","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeWedderburnGeneral.lean#L64-L70","doc":"The block product has dimension `(n+1)!`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.sum_dLambda_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.sum_dLambda_sq","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeWedderburnGeneral.lean#L59-L62","doc":"`Σ_λ d_λ² = (n+1)!` — SW-3, now unconditional at every `n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.finrank_blocks","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.finrank_blocks","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeWedderburnGeneral.lean#L47-L57","doc":"The block product has dimension `Σ_λ d_λ²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.finiteDimensional_hecke","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.finiteDimensional_hecke","kind":"theorem","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeWedderburnGeneral.lean#L39-L45","doc":"The Hecke algebra is finite-dimensional: the coset family is a finite spanning set. ","signatureChunk":0}]}